From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Contributor <contributor@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] launcher: define _CRT_RAND_S before including windows.h

rand_s is declared by <stdlib.h> only if _CRT_RAND_S is defined first.
MinGW-w64's <windows.h> includes <stdlib.h>, so defining the macro after
<windows.h> leaves rand_s undeclared and the launcher fails to compile for
*-windows-gnu targets (e.g. with an LLVM/MinGW cross toolchain on Linux or
macOS, where Bazel builds launcher.exe from source):

  launcher_util.cc:209:5: error: use of undeclared identifier 'rand_s'

Define it before any system header. No change for MSVC.
---
diff --git a/src/tools/launcher/util/launcher_util.cc b/src/tools/launcher/util/launcher_util.cc
index 70c8923..2f25737 100644
--- a/src/tools/launcher/util/launcher_util.cc
+++ b/src/tools/launcher/util/launcher_util.cc
@@ -12,13 +12,15 @@
 // See the License for the specific language governing permissions and
 // limitations under the License.
 
+// For rand_s function, https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/sxtz2fa8.aspx
+// Must precede every system header: MinGW-w64's <windows.h> includes <stdlib.h>.
+#define _CRT_RAND_S
+
 #ifndef WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
 #define WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
 #endif
 #include <windows.h>
 
-// For rand_s function, https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/sxtz2fa8.aspx
-#define _CRT_RAND_S
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <io.h>
 #include <stdarg.h>
